## PO rule

`karratha_sales_accessory_po_state_530(text)` maps `GP` plus eight digits to `po`. Every other value uses `sales_accessory_po_state`, which is not edited. Broome still classifies `GP10516751` as `other`.

A blank or `NONE` stays `blank`, so the tick is red (`po_not_raised`). `NO UPDATE`, `C&S ONLY` and `SELL ONLY` stay green: no purchase order is required. Any other non-GP text, including a short GP number, stays amber review. The 25 Oct file has no such row.

The plan reclassifies before `sales_accessory_ticks`. The Karratha read does the same from `po_number`. A before-write trigger stores that state on `karratha_sales_accessory_lines`. The manifested receipt payload is left as it is, so the same file sha stays idempotent. Match, manifest, preview, apply and readback are the same actions.

Importer bodies are unchanged: Broome `46d4b464c5c1800c8ada245fb2d33bd3`, Karratha `c70dc4234952dfb58cbc022c98bcecdb`. Writes stay on the 14450 tables. No vehicle, job, booking or auto-close. Department 135 is not edited.

## Sales page

Accessory, aftermarket, special and miscacc stay in the one notes list on that vehicle, grouped by PO, the same as Broome. Admin stays under the Admin heading. There is no second Karratha line. A GP number renders green. Only a blank PO renders Not raised.

